## 1. Public surface integrity — PASS

Status: PASS. Evidence: `v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/__init__.py:1-12` re-exports only `StreamIdObservation`, `GrowthWindowConfig`, `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window`, and `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError`; `__all__` is exactly those four names at `__init__.py:7-12`. `v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/test_public_surface.py:8-32` verifies the exact tuple, excludes `parsed_id`, and excludes `_`-prefixed names. The `errors` submodule is not in `__all__`. Remediation ask: none.

## 2. Spec faithfulness - StreamIdObservation — PASS

Status: PASS. Evidence: `v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/stream_observation.py:49-64` defines `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)` with fields ordered as `stream_name`, `stream_id`, `observation_ts_ms`, and `parsed_id()` returning the parsed tuple. `stream_observation.py:11-23` enforces stream-name type, non-empty value, no edge/internal whitespace, no path separator, and the allowed character set; `stream_observation.py:26-46` enforces exactly one separator and decimal non-negative stream-id components; `stream_observation.py:55-61` rejects non-int/bool and negative observation timestamps. Coverage evidence is `test_stream_observation_validation.py:13-83` and `test_stream_observation_parsed_id.py:11-30`. Remediation ask: none.

