# Phase 2E1.C.beta - Codex Review

Scope: REQ_0006 V2 trainer GPU parity service, stream-id growth windowing domain layer only. Codex did not modify any file under `v2/backend/`, did not read or write Redis, did not run the live trainer, did not deploy, and did not access network or secrets.

## 1. Public surface integrity — PASS

Evidence: `v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/__init__.py:1-12` exports exactly `StreamIdObservation`, `GrowthWindowConfig`, `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window`, and `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError`; `v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/test_public_surface.py:8-14` asserts the exact tuple. `parsed_id` and `_`-prefixed helpers are absent from `__all__` (`test_public_surface.py:26-32`), and Codex confirmed `errors` is not in `__all__`.

## 2. Spec faithfulness - StreamIdObservation — PASS

Evidence: `v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/stream_observation.py:49-64` defines the frozen slots dataclass with fields in spec order and exposes `parsed_id() -> tuple[int, int]`; `stream_observation.py:11-23` validates `stream_name`, `stream_observation.py:26-46` validates and parses the stream-id literal, and `stream_observation.py:55-61` rejects non-int/bool and negative `observation_ts_ms`. Coverage evidence: `test_stream_observation_validation.py:13-83` and `test_stream_observation_parsed_id.py:11-30` cover empty/whitespace/path/control names, malformed/signed/hex/float stream IDs, very large IDs, negative/non-int timestamps, frozen mutation, parsed tuple types, and bypassed-state parsing failure.

## 3. Spec faithfulness - GrowthWindowConfig — PASS

